/-
OnBytes/Tie/Pv/Keeps/BookModel.lean: in a dry run every opening that the verifier's routines note is
the opening of a tree of the book, and the book's trees keep shape, number and source: 355 routines
of OnBytes/Iop/, OnBytes/Model/ and OnBytes/Proof/.

Statements and proofs, made by the commands of OnBytes/Tie/Pv/Keeps/KeepsWalk.lean, one line for
each routine, in the order of OnBytes/Tie/Pv/Keeps/KeepsModel.lean. Inside this namespace KeepsM x
reads as `BookB` says (OnBytes/Tie/Pv/Keeps/BookKit.lean). keeps_had: the class is there already.
keeps_walk: the routine's text is unfolded and gone through. keeps_walk_fn: the same for a routine
that is written as a function of a state. keeps_walk_rec: by induction along the routine's own
recursion.
Of KeepsModel.lean's 394 names 355 stand here and 35 in BookKit.lean. Two others are Blk.setBook
and Blk.takeColumns, which do not have the property by themselves. Through the last two the commands
did not get: Blk.openTreesInto and Blk.openTrees: they take the book as an argument. BookKit.lean
has the first from a context whose book has grown out of that argument (`openTreesInto_book`); the
second is the first at an empty list of results and has no statement of its own.
Limits: those of OnBytes/Tie/Pv/Keeps/BookKit.lean. The statements in plain words are in
OnBytes/Tie/Pv/Keeps/BookBlocks.lean.
-/
